Built standalone, stdlib-only compress.py with both requested CLI modes, reversible record/alphabet packing, and a bzip2 fallback. The 44,267-byte corpus compresses to 16,778 bytes—a 62.0982% reduction, beating default zlib’s 22,390 bytes. Verified byte-identical restoration through the CLI and passed 108 additional round-trip tests. Registered assay.py reports the required correctness-gated size-reduction score.